(local Python / Node)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="90" y="380" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="9" value="stdin
JSON-RPC requests" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#1e88e5;strokeWidth=1.6;fontSize=10;fontColor=#000000;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="170" y="240" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="170" y="380" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="10" value="stdout
responses" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#43a047;strokeWidth=1.6;fontSize=10;fontColor=#000000;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="210" y="380" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="210" y="240" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="11" value="Used for filesystem, git, sqlite — tools that live on the host.

No network.   No auth.   Process lifecycle = transport lifecycle.
Doesn't count as one of our four patterns." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d4b600;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="470" width="390" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="12" value="Examples:
claude_desktop_config.json — type: 'stdio'
mcp dev / mcp run (Python SDK)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="580" width="390" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="13" value="Claude Desktop
(MCP host)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="540" y="180" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="14" value="MCP server
(your tools)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="540" y="380" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="15" value="GET /sse
opens SSE stream
(server → client)" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#43a047;strokeWidth=1.6;fontSize=10;fontColor=#000000;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="590" y="240" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="590" y="380" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="16" value="POST /messages
(client → server)" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#1e88e5;strokeWidth=1.6;fontSize=10;fontColor=#000000;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="670" y="380" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="670" y="240" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="17" value="Two endpoints, glued together.
SSE for server-to-client; separate POSTs for client-to-server.
Works but awkward to host (sticky sessions, two routes to manage)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff9e6;strokeColor=#d4b600;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="510" y="470" width="390" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="18" value="Examples:
Server-Sent Events transport, MCP spec v0.1
Used by early MCP servers (2024)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="510" y="580" width="390" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="19" value="Claude Desktop
(MCP host)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="990" y="180" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="20" value="MCP server
(your tools)" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="990" y="380" width="160" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="21" value="POST /mcp
request body" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#1e88e5;strokeWidth=1.6;fontSize=10;fontColor=#000000;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1070" y="240" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1070" y="380" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="22" value="response body
IS the SSE stream
(many progress events
 + final result)" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;strokeColor=#43a047;strokeWidth=1.6;fontSize=10;fontColor=#000000;labelBackgroundColor=#FFFFFF;fontStyle=1;dashed=1;dashPattern=4 4;" edge="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="1070" y="380" as="sourcePoint"/><mxPoint x="1070" y="240" as="targetPoint"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="23" value="Single endpoint.   The response body itself is an SSE stream.
One request can stream many progress events plus a final result.
Easy to host on Cloud Run, Vercel, anywhere that supports streaming." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f5e9;strokeColor=#43a047;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="960" y="470" width="390" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="24" value="Examples:
MCP spec 2025-03-26 onwards (current standard)
Claude Desktop, mcp.run, Cursor" style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#43a047;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="960" y="580" width="390" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="25" value="ALL THREE ARE SSE-SHAPED AT THE PROTOCOL LEVEL:   one request   →   many response events (progress + result).
The transport differs.   The protocol shape does not." style="rounded=1;arcSize=10;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f5e9;strokeColor=#43a047;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="690" width="1320" height="55" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
